<title>FRANCE: Quake jolts western Algeria.</title>
<headline>Quake jolts western Algeria.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>An earthquake measuring 4.7 on the open-ended Richter scale jolted western Algeria on Monday but there were no casualties or serious damage reported, said Algerian-state run radio.</p>
<p>The tremor at 4.50 p.m. (1550 GMT) rocked Relizane town and neighbouring villages, 250 km (156 miles) west of Algiers, and Chlef area, 150 km (90 miles) west of the Algerian capital, it said.</p>
<p>The quake's epicentre was registered by Algeria's seismological studies's centre 60 km (37.5 miles) west of Chlef.</p>
